# Vercel does not read .gitignore, so the deploy upload is trimmed here. The app being built
# (apps/web, the marketing + docs site) plus its TypeScript workspace deps (packages/*) are what's
# needed. Everything else — the Rust engine (455 MB of target), Move, the repo-root docs/ folder,
# and unrelated tooling — is excluded so the upload stays small and never aborts.
#
# IMPORTANT: anchor repo-root-only dirs with a leading slash. An unanchored entry like `docs`
# matches a `docs` directory at ANY depth, which silently strips apps/web/app/docs (the in-site
# docs route), apps/web/components/docs, and apps/web/content/docs from the build.

node_modules
.vercel

# heavy / irrelevant to the web build (repo-root only — note the leading slash)
/engine
/move
/gstack
/tmp
/docs
/scripts
/.github

# build artifacts (the Console and its deps are rebuilt on Vercel)
**/dist
**/target
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
